IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `oapa-nouns`
IMPORT `oapa-assaults`

-- Offences against the Person Act 1861 -- TESTS for oapa-assaults.l4 (sections 36 to
-- 47).  Every expected value was decided from the section's text before the assertion
-- was written, and is stated beside it.

§ `Tests: assaults`

§§ `Section 36`

-- obstructed divine service, obstructed a burial, struck or offered violence, arrested on
-- civil process, minister engaged, minister about to engage (to the offender's
-- knowledge), minister going to or returning from the rites (to the offender's knowledge)
`s36 obstructed divine service by force` MEANS `Conduct under section 36` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s36 obstructed a burial by threats` MEANS `Conduct under section 36` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s36 struck a minister engaged in the rites` MEANS `Conduct under section 36` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s36 arrested a minister engaged in the rites` MEANS `Conduct under section 36` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s36 struck a minister known to be about to officiate` MEANS `Conduct under section 36` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`s36 struck a minister known to be returning from the rites` MEANS `Conduct under section 36` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`s36 struck a minister not engaged and not known to be going to the rites` MEANS `Conduct under section 36` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s36 minister engaged but nothing done` MEANS `Conduct under section 36` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`s36 nothing` MEANS `Conduct under section 36` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `s 36: obstructing or assaulting a clergyman or other minister` `s36 obstructed divine service by force`
#ASSERT `s 36: obstructing or assaulting a clergyman or other minister` `s36 obstructed a burial by threats`
#ASSERT `s 36: obstructing or assaulting a clergyman or other minister` `s36 struck a minister engaged in the rites`
#ASSERT `s 36: obstructing or assaulting a clergyman or other minister` `s36 arrested a minister engaged in the rites`
#ASSERT `s 36: obstructing or assaulting a clergyman or other minister` `s36 struck a minister known to be about to officiate`
#ASSERT `s 36: obstructing or assaulting a clergyman or other minister` `s36 struck a minister known to be returning from the rites`
-- the striking limb needs the minister to be engaged, or known to be about to be / going
#ASSERT NOT (`s 36: obstructing or assaulting a clergyman or other minister` `s36 struck a minister not engaged and not known to be going to the rites`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 36: obstructing or assaulting a clergyman or other minister` `s36 minister engaged but nothing done`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 36: obstructing or assaulting a clergyman or other minister` `s36 nothing`)
#ASSERT `s 36: what the text calls the offence` EQUALS misdemeanor
#ASSERT `s 36: the sentences the text states` EQUALS LIST `imprisonment` (`for a term not exceeding` 24)

§§ `Section 37`

-- assaulted and struck, assaulted and wounded, the person was lawfully authorized, it was
-- on account of the preservation duty
`s37 struck` MEANS `Conduct under section 37` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`s37 wounded` MEANS `Conduct under section 37` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`s37 struck a person not authorized` MEANS `Conduct under section 37` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`s37 struck an authorized person, not on account of the preservation duty` MEANS `Conduct under section 37` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`s37 neither struck nor wounded` MEANS `Conduct under section 37` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE

#ASSERT `s 37: assaulting a person preserving a vessel or wreck` `s37 struck`
#ASSERT `s 37: assaulting a person preserving a vessel or wreck` `s37 wounded`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 37: assaulting a person preserving a vessel or wreck` `s37 struck a person not authorized`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 37: assaulting a person preserving a vessel or wreck` `s37 struck an authorized person, not on account of the preservation duty`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 37: assaulting a person preserving a vessel or wreck` `s37 neither struck nor wounded`)
#ASSERT `s 37: what the text calls the offence` EQUALS misdemeanor
-- seven years = 84 months
#ASSERT `s 37: the sentences the text states` EQUALS LIST `penal servitude` (`for a term not exceeding` 84)

§§ `Section 38`

-- assaulted a person, intent to resist or prevent the person's own lawful apprehension,
-- intent to resist or prevent another person's
`s38 assault, own apprehension` MEANS `Conduct under section 38` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`s38 assault, another's apprehension` MEANS `Conduct under section 38` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`s38 assault, no such intent` MEANS `Conduct under section 38` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s38 intent, no assault` MEANS `Conduct under section 38` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE

#ASSERT `s 38: assault with intent to resist or prevent lawful apprehension` `s38 assault, own apprehension`
#ASSERT `s 38: assault with intent to resist or prevent lawful apprehension` `s38 assault, another's apprehension`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 38: assault with intent to resist or prevent lawful apprehension` `s38 assault, no such intent`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 38: assault with intent to resist or prevent lawful apprehension` `s38 intent, no assault`)
#ASSERT `s 38: what the text calls the offence` EQUALS misdemeanor
#ASSERT `s 38: the sentences the text states` EQUALS LIST `imprisonment` (`for a term not exceeding` 24)

§§ `Section 39`

-- beat or used violence or a threat, intent to deter/hinder/compel in a market, person had
-- care of the goods in transit, intent to stop the conveyance
`s39 violence to hinder a sale` MEANS `Conduct under section 39` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s39 violence to a carrier, intent to stop conveyance` MEANS `Conduct under section 39` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`s39 intent to stop conveyance, but the person was not in charge of the goods` MEANS `Conduct under section 39` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`s39 carrier, violence, no intent` MEANS `Conduct under section 39` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`s39 intent but no violence` MEANS `Conduct under section 39` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE

#ASSERT `s 39: violence to obstruct the sale or conveyance of grain` `s39 violence to hinder a sale`
#ASSERT `s 39: violence to obstruct the sale or conveyance of grain` `s39 violence to a carrier, intent to stop conveyance`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 39: violence to obstruct the sale or conveyance of grain` `s39 intent to stop conveyance, but the person was not in charge of the goods`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 39: violence to obstruct the sale or conveyance of grain` `s39 carrier, violence, no intent`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 39: violence to obstruct the sale or conveyance of grain` `s39 intent but no violence`)
#ASSERT `s 39: what the text calls the offence` EQUALS `no classification stated`
#ASSERT `s 39: how the text says the offence is tried` EQUALS `summarily before justices of the peace`
-- three months
#ASSERT `s 39: the sentences the text states` EQUALS LIST `imprisonment` (`for a term not exceeding` 3)
-- the proviso: one punished under the section cannot be punished again under another law
#ASSERT `s 39: the person cannot be punished for the same offence under any other law` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 39: the person cannot be punished for the same offence under any other law` FALSE)

§§ `Section 40`

-- unlawfully, with force hindered or prevented a seaman/keelman/caster from working, beat
-- or used violence to such a person, intent to hinder or prevent them from working
`s40 unlawfully hindered with force` MEANS `Conduct under section 40` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s40 hindered with force, not unlawfully` MEANS `Conduct under section 40` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s40 beat, intent to hinder, not stated as unlawful` MEANS `Conduct under section 40` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`s40 beat, no intent` MEANS `Conduct under section 40` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`s40 nothing` MEANS `Conduct under section 40` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `s 40: violence to hinder a seaman, keelman or caster` `s40 unlawfully hindered with force`
-- "unlawfully and with force": force without "unlawfully" does not satisfy the first limb
#ASSERT NOT (`s 40: violence to hinder a seaman, keelman or caster` `s40 hindered with force, not unlawfully`)
-- the beating limb has no "unlawfully" in the text
#ASSERT `s 40: violence to hinder a seaman, keelman or caster` `s40 beat, intent to hinder, not stated as unlawful`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 40: violence to hinder a seaman, keelman or caster` `s40 beat, no intent`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 40: violence to hinder a seaman, keelman or caster` `s40 nothing`)
#ASSERT `s 40: what the text calls the offence` EQUALS `no classification stated`
#ASSERT `s 40: how the text says the offence is tried` EQUALS `summarily before justices of the peace`
#ASSERT `s 40: the sentences the text states` EQUALS LIST `imprisonment` (`for a term not exceeding` 3)
#ASSERT `s 40: the person cannot be punished for the same offence under any other law` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 40: the person cannot be punished for the same offence under any other law` FALSE)

§§ `Sections 41, 43 and 46`

#ASSERT `s 41: blank in this text` EQUALS "Section 41 shows only its number and a row of dots; there is nothing to encode."
#ASSERT `s 46: blank in this text` EQUALS "Section 46 shows only its number and a row of dots; there is nothing to encode."

§§ `Section 42`

-- unlawfully assaulted or beat another person, a complaint by or on behalf of the party aggrieved
`s42 assault and complaint` MEANS `Conduct under section 42` OF TRUE, TRUE
`s42 assault, no complaint` MEANS `Conduct under section 42` OF TRUE, FALSE
`s42 complaint, no assault` MEANS `Conduct under section 42` OF FALSE, TRUE

#ASSERT `s 42: two justices may hear and determine a common assault or battery` `s42 assault and complaint`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 42: two justices may hear and determine a common assault or battery` `s42 assault, no complaint`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 42: two justices may hear and determine a common assault or battery` `s42 complaint, no assault`)
#ASSERT `s 42: what the text calls the offence` EQUALS `no classification stated`
#ASSERT `s 42: how the text says the offence is tried` EQUALS `summarily before justices of the peace`
-- 6 months' imprisonment; or a fine which with costs does not exceed £200; or, on
-- non-payment, up to 6 months' imprisonment
#ASSERT `s 42: the sentences the text states` EQUALS LIST `imprisonment` (`for a term not exceeding` 6), `a fine, with any costs, not exceeding` 200, `imprisonment in default of paying a fine and costs` (`for a term not exceeding` 6)
-- the £200 ceiling covers the fine TOGETHER WITH costs: boundary on each side
#ASSERT `s 42: the fine together with the costs is within the maximum` 200 0
#ASSERT `s 42: the fine together with the costs is within the maximum` 150 50
#ASSERT `s 42: the fine together with the costs is within the maximum` 199 1
#ASSERT NOT (`s 42: the fine together with the costs is within the maximum` 200 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 42: the fine together with the costs is within the maximum` 150 51)
-- 6 months is within, 7 is not
#ASSERT `s 42: the imprisonment is within the maximum` 6
#ASSERT `s 42: the imprisonment is within the maximum` 0
#ASSERT NOT (`s 42: the imprisonment is within the maximum` 7)

§§ `Section 43`

#ASSERT `s 43: only the title survives in this text` EQUALS "Section 43 keeps its title but its text is a row of dots; the title names an offence the text no longer states, and nothing is encoded."

§§ `Section 44`

-- a complaint under s 42 or 43, heard on the merits, deemed not proved, found justified,
-- found so trifling as not to merit punishment, dismissed
`s44 not proved, dismissed` MEANS `Dismissal under section 44` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`s44 justified, dismissed` MEANS `Dismissal under section 44` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`s44 trifling, dismissed` MEANS `Dismissal under section 44` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`s44 dismissed on none of the three grounds` MEANS `Dismissal under section 44` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`s44 not proved but not dismissed` MEANS `Dismissal under section 44` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s44 no complaint by the party aggrieved` MEANS `Dismissal under section 44` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`s44 not heard on the merits` MEANS `Dismissal under section 44` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

#ASSERT `s 44: a certificate of dismissal is owed to the person complained against` `s44 not proved, dismissed`
#ASSERT `s 44: a certificate of dismissal is owed to the person complained against` `s44 justified, dismissed`
#ASSERT `s 44: a certificate of dismissal is owed to the person complained against` `s44 trifling, dismissed`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 44: a certificate of dismissal is owed to the person complained against` `s44 dismissed on none of the three grounds`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 44: a certificate of dismissal is owed to the person complained against` `s44 not proved but not dismissed`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 44: a certificate of dismissal is owed to the person complained against` `s44 no complaint by the party aggrieved`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 44: a certificate of dismissal is owed to the person complained against` `s44 not heard on the merits`)
#ASSERT `s 44: when the certificate is due` EQUALS "forthwith"

§§ `Section 45`

-- a complaint of the kind in s 44, obtained a certificate, convicted and paid the whole
-- amount adjudged, convicted and suffered the imprisonment awarded
`s45 obtained a certificate` MEANS `Release under section 45` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s45 convicted and paid` MEANS `Release under section 45` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`s45 convicted and served the imprisonment` MEANS `Release under section 45` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`s45 convicted, not yet paid or served` MEANS `Release under section 45` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s45 certificate but no complaint of that kind` MEANS `Release under section 45` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `s 45: the person is released from all further proceedings, civil or criminal, for the same cause` `s45 obtained a certificate`
#ASSERT `s 45: the person is released from all further proceedings, civil or criminal, for the same cause` `s45 convicted and paid`
#ASSERT `s 45: the person is released from all further proceedings, civil or criminal, for the same cause` `s45 convicted and served the imprisonment`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 45: the person is released from all further proceedings, civil or criminal, for the same cause` `s45 convicted, not yet paid or served`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 45: the person is released from all further proceedings, civil or criminal, for the same cause` `s45 certificate but no complaint of that kind`)

§§ `Section 47`

-- assaulted a person, the assault occasioned actual bodily harm
`s47 assault occasioning actual bodily harm` MEANS `Conduct under section 47` OF TRUE, TRUE
`s47 assault, no actual bodily harm` MEANS `Conduct under section 47` OF TRUE, FALSE
`s47 actual bodily harm, no assault` MEANS `Conduct under section 47` OF FALSE, TRUE

#ASSERT `s 47: assault occasioning actual bodily harm` `s47 assault occasioning actual bodily harm`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 47: assault occasioning actual bodily harm` `s47 assault, no actual bodily harm`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 47: assault occasioning actual bodily harm` `s47 actual bodily harm, no assault`)
#ASSERT `s 47: what the text calls the offence` EQUALS `no classification stated`
#ASSERT `s 47: how the text says the offence is tried` EQUALS `on indictment`
#ASSERT `s 47: the sentences the text states` EQUALS LIST `penal servitude` `for a term the text does not state`

§§ `Sections 48 to 54`

#ASSERT `ss 48, 49, 50, 52, 53 and 54: blank in this text` EQUALS "Sections 48, 49, 50, 52, 53 and 54 show only their numbers and a row of dots; there is nothing to encode.  The text has no row for section 51."
